<title>TURKEY: Turkey sets 2-year bond auction for Thursday.</title>
<headline>Turkey sets 2-year bond auction for Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish central bank said the Treasury would auction on Thursday two-year, inflation-indexed bonds with three-month interest payments after it last sold 133 trillion lira of similar bonds on April 8 at 22 percent risk premium above inflation.</p>
<p>The treasury faces 34.7 trillion lira of bond redemption on May 1 and some 130 trillion lira t-bill repayments on May 7.</p>
<p>Details of Thursday's auction are as follows:</p>
<p>    Maturity    : May 2, 1999</p>
<p>    Amount	: -</p>
<p>    Coupon	: -</p>
<p>Auction date: May 1, 1997</p>
<p>Value date  : May 2, 1997</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75</p>
</text>
